      "before": [
        {
          "eyebrow": "All the way from Japan",
          "heading": {
            "lead": "The dress",
            "accent": "came with them."
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            "This wonderful shoot began at a hotel in Amalfi. As I understood it, they had arrived from Japan only the day before, so the jet lag was severe. But what I remember most clearly about that morning is the wedding dress.",
            "We were making post-wedding photographs, and they had brought their actual wedding dress all the way from Japan. It made such an impression that I have been telling people about this shoot ever since."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "spreads",
      "eyebrow": "02 / A welcome from the town",
      "heading": {
        "lead": "“Auguri!”",
        "accent": "at every turn."
      },
      "frameIds": [
        "cnr0486",
        "cnr0504",
        "cnr0509",
        "cnr0594",
        "cnr0710",
        "cnr0825",
        "cnr0887",
        "cnr0958",
        "cnr1073",
        "cnr1159",
        "cnr1172",
        "cnr1307"
      ],
      "before": [
        {
          "eyebrow": "A welcome from the town",
          "heading": {
            "lead": "“Auguri!”",
            "accent": "at every turn."
          },
          "paragraphs": [
            "I love starting at six in the morning. We walked through Amalfi towards Atrani to catch the first rays as the sun appeared from behind the mountain. I wanted us to be there at exactly that moment.",
            "The dress took up almost the whole road. Every passing car—and I do mean every one—stopped so that people could admire it and call out “Auguri!”, the Italian way of offering congratulations. It was quite a procession.",
            "We had barely walked any distance before collecting enough compliments for the next three weeks. In Atrani we stopped for photographs at sunrise, but the congratulations kept coming. People here know me, and the locals who were already walking their dogs or getting ready for the day greeted us on foot and from their cars. Again and again: “Auguri!”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "dissolve",
      "eyebrow": "03 / Room for a little silliness",
      "heading": {
        "lead": "The formal portraits,",
        "accent": "and the laughter."
      },
      "frameIds": [
        "cnr1327",
